 loc='\U0001f4cd Near Borger / Drouwen, on the Hondsrug \u00b7 Small bog site \u00b7 Small site',
 desc='The <b>Meindersveen</b> is a small raised-bog remnant in the woods on the Hondsrug near Borger. It is named after an owner or user \u2014 such personal names are common for small Drenthe bogs, because the <b>peat rights</b> to a bog sometimes belonged to a single family who cut their own fuel there generation after generation. Because the parcel was small and the peat thin, that cutting stopped before everything was gone, and a <b>bog-moss core</b> survived. Today the bog is embedded in conifer plantation, and that is at once its greatest problem: the surrounding wood <b>transpires water</b> and pulls the water table down, whereas raised bog needs a permanently high, stable water level. Management has therefore <b>felled trees and dammed ditches</b> in the buffer zone. The core now carries <b>bog moss, cotton grass, small cranberry and sundew</b> again, and in spring moor frogs breed in the wettest hollows.',
